# Context root for the production image (see ./Dockerfile). Docker reads .dockerignore from the
# CONTEXT root, so frontend/.dockerignore does not apply to a repo-root build — without this file
# the host's node_modules is copied over each stage's freshly-installed tree and the build dies on
# esbuild's platform check (host binaries are darwin-arm64; the image is linux).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.github
.claude
docs
security
scripts
*.md

# Never let a real environment file into an image layer. The `**/` prefixes are load-bearing:
# a bare `.env` matches ONLY the context root, so frontend/.env.local — which README tells every
# developer to create with their real Auth0 values — would be copied by `COPY frontend/ ./` into
# the frontend stage's layer. The final image would not carry it, but `--target frontend`,
# `docker history` and any exported BuildKit cache would.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
